
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.MinEventDelay(Delay: number)`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`llMinEventDelay(float Delay);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Set the minimum time between events being handled.</p>
  <p>Defaults and minimums vary by the event type, see <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LSL_Delay" target="_blank">LSL Delay</a>.</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>number</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>float</span></td>
          <td>Delay / delay</td>
          <td>time in seconds</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>script</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">125</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <p>Minimum delay is maintained between state changes.</p>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function main()
    ll.MinEventDelay(5.0)
end
function LLEvents.touch(events)
    local detected = #events
    ll.Say(0, "Touched.")  --Without the event delay set touch would cause the screen to fill 
--with the word "Touched" in a split second if you held the mouse button down.
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        llMinEventDelay(5.0);
    }
    touch(integer detected)
    {
        llSay(0, "Touched.");//Without the event delay set touch would cause the screen to fill 
                             //with the word "Touched" in a split second if you held the mouse button down.
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>Where as, if in one object you place this script (for the sake of fun call the object &quot;Sandy Powell&quot;). -</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`function LLEvents.touch(events)
    local detected = #events
    ll.Say(0, "Can you hear me mother?")  --Northern English accent. Catch phase of Sandy Powell (comedian).
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    touch(integer detected)
    {
        llSay(0, "Can you hear me mother?"); //Northern English accent. Catch phase of Sandy Powell (comedian).
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>and this in another object called &quot;Mother&quot; -</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function main()
    ll.MinEventDelay(5.0)
    ll.Listen(0, "Sandy Powell", "", "")
end
function LLEvents.listen(chan, name, id, msg)
    ll.Say(0, "Eh?")
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        llMinEventDelay(5.0);
        llListen(0, "Sandy Powell", "", "");
    }
    listen(integer chan, string name, key id, string msg)
    {
        llSay(0, "Eh?");
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>the result in chat is as follows -</p>
  <p>[12:51] Sandy Powell: Can you hear me mother?
